                            <span class="sub-title" style="color: black !important;text-align: start !important;">Veterinary surgeon</span>

                        </div>
                        <p style="color: black !important;">Caring for your cat's health involves several necessary expenses:</p>


                        <p style="color: black !important;" class="py-3">Vaccinations are essential, typically costing between €25 to €50 each, depending on your location. Additionally, getting a microchip for your cat can range from €25 to €35 per kitten. For international travel, a rabies vaccination is mandatory, usually priced at €25 to €40 per kitten. Many breeders choose to spay or neuter their cats to prevent unexpected litters, with costs varying from €100 to €150 per cat. A passport is also required for all cats, priced between €15 to €30 per cat. Regular deworming is recommended three times during the kitten period. It's common to have the parents tested for diseases like FIV/FELV and HCM/PKD, which can cost between €100 to €150 per cat, depending on the breed and veterinarian. Some breeders may also choose to have X-rays done.</p>


                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-6 order-2-class d-flex ">
                    <img src="/webassets/images/elements/sergion-43.png" class="" alt="img">
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

</section>

