                        </div>
                        <p style="color: black !important;">Additionally, other factors come into play: the kittens you purchase are of show quality, with bloodlines from parents and grandparents of exceptional breeding standards. Moreover, there are additional costs such as fuel for transportation and the time invested in caring for these precious pedigree cats. As a result, it is evident that the expenses for a purebred cat or kitten can be quite significant.</p>


                        <p style="color: black !important;" class="pt-5">Also keep in mind that each cattery makes its own prices. These prices are greatly influenced by the pedigree and lineage of the cats, the accolades and awards their ancestors have achieved at prestigious shows, and the rarity or uniqueness of their breed. Factors such as coat colour and pattern, eye colour, and even personality traits that are highly desired in the feline world can also significantly influence these prices.    </p>


